  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-1,1]?$\n\n- $-1<0<\\frac{1}{2}<1$\n- ${-2,-1,0,1}$\n- ${-1,0,2}$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<\u2026<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-1,1]$ since $-2$ does not belong to $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of  $[-1,1]$ since $2$ does not belong to $[-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
